---
layout: base.njk
title: Book a consultation
description: Booking is by email. Send Sarah a short message and she'll reply to arrange a time that suits you.
---

{#- No contactFooter in the front matter: leaving it unset selects the compact dark footer. -#}
{% set steps = [
  "You email Sarah — a couple of lines about where you are is plenty",
  "She replies within one working day with a few times",
  "You pick one, and that's your free 20-minute intro call"
] %}
<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-head__title">Book a consultation</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lead">
    Booking is by email. Send Sarah a message and she'll reply to arrange a time that suits you.
  </p>
</div>
<div class="book-panel">
  {#- An ol: three steps in a fixed order, so a screen reader announces "list, 3
      items". The numbers are spans, not ::marker, because they need their own
      colour and weight — and no aria-hidden, they are content. -#}
  <ol class="book-steps">
    {%- for step in steps %}
      <li class="book-step">
        <span class="book-step__number">{{ loop.index }}</span>{{ step }}
      </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
  {#- TODO-SARAH: the dedicated email address — briefing section 6, question 4.
      Two lines change when we have it: this href becomes
      mailto:ADDRESS?subject=Consultation%20enquiry, and the span below becomes
      the address.

      Do not make this a valid mailto: in the meantime. mailto:TODO-SARAH-… is
      valid, so it opens a compose window addressed to nonsense — a silent
      failure. A non-URL 404s instead, and the marker survives into _site. -#}
  <a class="button" href="TODO-SARAH-email-address">Email Sarah to book</a>
  {#- The address must be readable, selectable text: a mailto: on a device with
      no mail client does nothing visible. Plain text, not a second mailto:,
      which would give a screen reader two adjacent links to the same place. -#}
  <p class="book-panel__address">
    Opens your email app, addressed to <span class="book-panel__email">TODO-SARAH — email address</span>
  </p>
</div>
